From bc5e77f582fe0b12a33c3c6ac62b39e305945470 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 05:55:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/31] Report the liked-songs sync outcome instead of failing
 silently

A liked-songs sync can decline to run (not signed in, category disabled,
cooldown) or fail against YouTube without anything visible changing, which
makes "the refresh did nothing" indistinguishable from "the refresh worked
and the order is still wrong". SYNC_DEBUG is a compile-time false, so the
logs say nothing either.

SyncState now carries lastLikedSongsResult, set on every exit path of the
liked sync, and pull-to-refresh on the Liked screen shows it in a snackbar:
either "Synced N liked songs" or the specific reason it stopped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019qFVKGXMsRYppSVGRXPgBQ
