From 1aafef6e9b7961ee1aba3daf550b69026e048679 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 07:59:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/31] Fix the Discord login hanging, and add a manual token
 fallback

Two problems, both mine.

The token check ran once, from onPageFinished. Discord is a single-page
app: it finishes loading the document and writes its token some
unpredictable moment afterwards, with no further page loads to trigger
another check. When the check lost that race there was no retry, so the
screen sat on a fully loaded Discord looking like it had frozen. It now
polls every 500ms for 30 seconds and stops as soon as a token arrives.

The WebView reference was also a plain local rather than state, so it was
null after any recomposition - which quietly disabled the back handler.

Separately, Discord does not always cooperate with an embedded browser at
all; a captcha it declines to render leaves no way forward. Pasting the
token directly always works, so Settings now offers that as a way out
instead of a dead end. The donor fork had this and I dropped it when
rebuilding the screen.

