From 31c4cd15f7738a5dc1aa223ebf5f687633eb232b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 08:53:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 24/31] Add a frosted glass player background

A new option alongside the existing ones, not a replacement for any of
them: the album art blurred past recognition, with a soft scrim over it.

The blur comes from fetching the artwork at 18px and letting it stretch
across the screen rather than from a large blur radius. It looks the
same, costs almost nothing, and works below Android 12 - where
Modifier.blur silently does nothing, which is why the existing Blur
option is hidden on those versions.

Also an optional "match text to the artwork" switch for the backgrounds
that are drawn from the cover. It measures the same tiny bitmap the
background is drawn from and puts dark text over pale covers, light text
over dark ones, using Rec. 709 luminance weights rather than a plain RGB
mean - a saturated blue cover reads as dark to the eye while a naive
average calls it mid-grey, and the text would come out the wrong colour.

Until the artwork has been measured the theme's own answer is used, so a
track change never flashes text in a colour it is about to abandon.
