From 25b8f379b9baa4f33ccfee1d22b00b01fe9a8c5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 09:06:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/31] Turn the home search into a field, and thin out the top
 bar

The search was a magnifying glass in a row of five near-identical icons,
which is a poor signpost for the thing most people open the app to do.
It is now a field running the width of the bar. Tapping it opens the same
search component as before - nothing about search itself changed - but it
reads as somewhere to type.

The logo sits slightly further in, and can be turned off entirely under
Appearance, in which case the field runs to the left edge.

History moves to Settings, next to the other library entries, and the
local media button is gone from the bar: it only ever navigated to
settings/local, which is already listed on the settings screen a few rows
below where History now is.
