From d91448588026cd7b85dfa6d0d45a75fe3740372e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 09:59:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 27/31] Import player layouts from the layout editor

Settings -> Appearance -> Player layout takes a file from the standalone
editor. The portrait player's title block, progress block and transport
row are now emitted in the order the file gives, and hidden if it says
to hide them.

Parsed with org.json rather than kotlinx.serialization: the :app module
does not apply the serialization plugin, and pulling in a compiler plugin
and runtime to read one small file is a poor trade when org.json ships
with Android.

The parser assumes nothing. Every field falls back to the built-in value
if it is missing, malformed or out of range; unknown block ids are
dropped; a block the file never mentions comes back with its defaults
rather than vanishing. A file is validated before it is stored, so a bad
one cannot leave the player in a state the user has to reinstall to
escape, and there is a reset either way.

Two deliberate refusals: a layout claiming a newer schema is rejected
rather than guessed at, and the transport row is drawn whatever the file
says - hiding the play button leaves a player that cannot be paused from
its own screen, and a JSON file is not where anyone should discover that.

Not yet honoured: free placement, artwork size and per-block scale. Those
need the artwork and action row lifted out of their current parents,
which is a bigger change than this one and better made on its own.
